==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Pegasa, type ν''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Divine Pegasa ν''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Pegasa is a fairly middling unit. She has a high range of 450, below-average DPS, and somewhat mediocre survivability. Her [[Weaken]] against [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] and [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating enemies]] can be quite useful: with nearly 100% uptime, she's capable of keeping aggressive target traits at bay from a relatively safe distance. However, her performance against Zombies is not ideal because her poor health prevents her from tanking much damage from Zombies that burrow into her. Despite this, she outranges most common Floating and Zombie threats seen in [[Stories of Legend]], as well as those in early-mid-[[Uncanny Legends]]. Her performance as a debuffer against her target traits is fairly average overall, but she has no use outside of that niche.

Her spirit, on the other hand, is amazing, as it [[Slow|Slows]] all enemies for 6 seconds. This, along with its 800 range and standard 45,900 damage, makes it incredibly powerful whenever you're in a pinch. However, it doesn't have [[Zombie Killer]], so be careful when using it around Zombie enemies.

==='''True Form'''===
[[Massive Damage]]. This single ability completely changes Pegasa's role in battle, now packing a very decent punch with each attack. At Lv.30, she deals 95,200 damage against Zombies/Floating (151,200 at Lv.50), and has an effective ~17,960 DPS (28,520 DPS at Lv.50). There is not a lot of elaboration needed to explain why this alone is such a worthwhile upgrade.

Pegasa's HP has also been improved, which allows her to better utilize each of her knockbacks, especially when Zombies burrow into her. This works doubly so with Massive Damage: when she attacks after getting forcefully repositioned, she'll end up severely crippling whatever was targeting her. If that wasn't enough, her spirit also has a better Slow duration to ward off threats even longer.

Definitely a worthwhile True Form.

